TEST 1 — SEASONALITY OVERLAY (do cycles trace the same shape in halving-time?)
  cross-cycle correlation of the halving-aligned price path: E1-E2 0.82, E1-E3 0.72, E2-E3 0.61  (mean 0.72)
  placebo (random-offset alignment): mean corr 0.02, P(random >= halving alignment) = 2.8%

TEST 2 — PLACEBO ANCHORS (is the tightness halving-specific or any 4-year clock?)
  tops' days-after-anchor RANGE:  halving 21d   election 68d   fixed-4yr 1423d
  random 4-year clocks: median range 71d, P(random clock <= halving's 21d) = 0.0%
  -> the halving anchor is tighter than 100% of random 4-year clocks

